    <item>
      <title>From: Lorie, To: Elijah H. Chandler</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/1921/05/28/213/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 May 1921 23:37:35 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/1921/05/28/213/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_17382407_0001.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140414_17382407_0001&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_17382407_0001.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_17383190_0002.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140414_17383190_0002&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://107.170.91.122/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140414_17383190_0002.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Lorie, To: Elijah H. Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Pana, Illinois on May 28, 1921&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mr. Elijah H. Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pana, Illinois&lt;br&gt;
Dear Folks,&lt;br&gt;
We are going to try and make it and hop off tomorrow a.m. Will try and be there tomorrow night but do not know for sure. It may be Monday a.m.&lt;br&gt;
Love to all,&lt;br&gt;
Lorie&lt;br&gt;
Also, it is quite a city. Tell Grace and Ruby, if there, to go along.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
